Chapter: VmRunner
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter CCE
  cites Works chapter DevHypervisor

 VmRunner boots a compiled CDX binary inside a VMX guest and captures
 the serial output. Replaces run-for-sweep.ps1. The guest runs until
 HLT or the exit limit is reached. Serial output is collected from
 the virtual COM1 port.

 To vm-run-cdx gives VmRunResult,
   running a CDX binary and returning its serial output as text.

 We say:

Section: Types

  VmRunOutput = record {
    vro-text : Text,
    vro-halted : Boolean,
    vro-exit-count : Integer
  }

Section: Run

  vm-run-cdx : List Integer, Integer -> VmRunOutput
  vm-run-cdx (cdx-bytes) (revision-id) =
    let cfg = GuestConfig { entry-point = 1048576, stack-size = 65536, memory-mb = 256 }
    in let result = vm-setup-and-run-with-serial cfg revision-id cdx-bytes []
    in let output-text = vm-serial-get-output (result.vfr-devices.vd-com1)
    in VmRunOutput {
      vro-text = output-text,
      vro-halted = when result.vfr-status is VmHalted -> True is otherwise -> False,
      vro-exit-count = 0
    }

  vm-run-cdx-with-input : List Integer, List Integer, Integer -> VmRunOutput
  vm-run-cdx-with-input (cdx-bytes) (stdin-bytes) (revision-id) =
    let cfg = GuestConfig { entry-point = 1048576, stack-size = 65536, memory-mb = 256 }
    in let result = vm-setup-and-run-with-serial cfg revision-id cdx-bytes stdin-bytes
    in let output-text = vm-serial-get-output (result.vfr-devices.vd-com1)
    in VmRunOutput {
      vro-text = output-text,
      vro-halted = when result.vfr-status is VmHalted -> True is otherwise -> False,
      vro-exit-count = 0
    }

